      "status": "In Progress",
      "notes": "Supported by TSET funding Telehealth consultant costs to develop and implement tools for distant monitoring, such as thermograms, cardiac monitoring, etc. The OCTSI/OSCTR has built an Evaluation Core which provides external Evaluation for OCTSI/OSCTR Programs and has also done multiple evaluation programs for tribal facilities, the Tribal Epidemiology Unit, and other organizations. Dr. Janis Campbell is an Associate Professor at the adjacent OUHSC and she and her unit will be hired to perform evaluation services for the TIHO. The approximate $6.4M requested will finish out the 2nd and 3rd floors of the Advanced Human Imaging Center for which over $7.45M is already raised as matching funds. These renovations include all architectural and design services, site prep, contractor activitities, plumbing, electrical, technology, furniture, fixtures and equipment. Detailed bids and cost estimates are available as needed."
